---
layout: null
permalink: /sitemap.xml
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  The sitemap, written by this page in each language's build and merged into ONE file at the
  root by _plugins/sitemap_merge.rb (jekyll-sitemap is not used: under jekyll-polyglot it wrote
  the Italian pages without their /it/ prefix, in a second sitemap at /it/sitemap.xml).

  Why each language lists its own pages: a build sees only the documents of its language
  (jekyll-polyglot hides the others, and a page left out of a language by `lang-exclusive`
  does not exist in that build at all), so the English build lists the English pages and
  the Italian one the Italian pages, among them the articles that exist in Italian only.
  This is why this page is NOT in `exclude_from_localization`. The merge takes the <url>
  entries of /it/sitemap.xml into /sitemap.xml and deletes /it/sitemap.xml; an entry listed
  by both builds (a page without a version in the other language, shown there as a fallback
  copy) is kept once.

  Each entry is computed like the page's own head (_includes/head.html), by the same
  _includes/lang-url.html: <loc> is its canonical URL, and the hreflang alternates are the
  <link rel="alternate"> set of the page (a page of one language only lists itself and
  x-default). script/checks/sitemap.rb compares both against the built pages.

  Left out: noindex pages (the legal drafts, the 404 page), `sitemap: false` pages, and
  everything that is not an HTML page (feeds, the sitemap itself, /_redirects, assets).
  <lastmod> is `last_modified_at` or the date of the document, and is left out for a page
  with neither (a collection document without a date gets the build time as its date: that is
  not when it changed, so it is not listed). The variables are prefixed (sm_).

  The URLs of the xhtml:link elements are wrapped in static_href: jekyll-polyglot would
  otherwise put /it/ on the English ones in the Italian build.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign sm_origin = site.url | append: site.baseurl -%}
{%- assign sm_docs = site.pages | concat: site.documents -%}
{%- assign sm_built = site.time | date_to_xmlschema -%}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9" xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
{%- for sm_doc in sm_docs -%}
  {%- assign sm_url = sm_doc.url -%}
  {%- assign sm_last = sm_url | slice: -1 -%}
  {%- assign sm_ext = sm_url | slice: -5, 5 -%}
  {%- if sm_last != "/" and sm_ext != ".html" -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if sm_url == "/404.html" or sm_doc.noindex or sm_doc.sitemap == false -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign sm_own = sm_doc.lang | default: site.active_lang -%}
  {%- capture sm_loc %}{% include lang-url.html lang=sm_own page=sm_doc %}{% endcapture -%}
  {%- assign sm_loc = sm_loc | strip -%}
  {%- if sm_loc == "" -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- capture sm_default %}{% include lang-url.html lang=site.default_lang page=sm_doc %}{% endcapture -%}
  {%- assign sm_default = sm_default | strip | default: sm_loc -%}
  {%- assign sm_lastmod = sm_doc.last_modified_at | default: sm_doc.date -%}
  {%- if sm_lastmod -%}{%- assign sm_lastmod = sm_lastmod | date_to_xmlschema -%}{%- if sm_lastmod == sm_built -%}{%- assign sm_lastmod = nil -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endif %}
<url>
  <loc>{{ sm_origin | append: sm_loc | xml_escape }}</loc>
  {%- if sm_lastmod %}
  <lastmod>{{ sm_lastmod }}</lastmod>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- for sm_lang in site.languages -%}
    {%- capture sm_alt %}{% include lang-url.html lang=sm_lang page=sm_doc %}{% endcapture -%}
    {%- assign sm_alt = sm_alt | strip -%}
    {%- if sm_alt != "" %}
  <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="{{ sm_lang }}" {% static_href %}href="{{ sm_origin | append: sm_alt | xml_escape }}"{% endstatic_href %} />
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor %}
  <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" {% static_href %}href="{{ sm_origin | append: sm_default | xml_escape }}"{% endstatic_href %} />
</url>
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
